                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d9cd4499-89e2-3e2d-a35e-bfb01c211b40",
                        "entry_id": "8ebeb3da-7361-3df3-8452-3dbf19c9c3be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To gird too closely."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "23dbe579-83b3-4d29-a7d1-26ef0329c26a",
                                "sense_id": "d9cd4499-89e2-3e2d-a35e-bfb01c211b40",
                                "text": "Yes, and all wholesome herbs, and all fresh dews, by your violent and hidebound frost; but, when the gentle west winds shall open the fruitful bosom of the earth , thus overgirded by your imprisonment , then the flowers put forth and spring, and then the sun shall scatter the mists, and the manuring hand of the tiller shall root up all that burdens the soil, without thank to your bondage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9123b20-93cd-401b-9168-332da8e2ce74",
                                "sense_id": "d9cd4499-89e2-3e2d-a35e-bfb01c211b40",
                                "text": "Perhaps the most important thing to remember, however, is don't overgird. Girding one's loins too tightly can lead to loss of circulation and, in extreme cases, loss of a loin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e0e62ad-2280-44af-9456-43790aaec9fc",
                                "sense_id": "d9cd4499-89e2-3e2d-a35e-bfb01c211b40",
                                "text": "The flaw with Locke's model is that his identification of black aestheticism was overgirded by the ferment of a single historical moment."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67540075-77c9-3108-88e7-f8a26fe4fff2",
                        "entry_id": "8ebeb3da-7361-3df3-8452-3dbf19c9c3be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To encircle; to gird over."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebae0601-e591-40f6-8655-a053da1067a0",
                                "sense_id": "67540075-77c9-3108-88e7-f8a26fe4fff2",
                                "text": "She is dressed in a long, overgirt Ionic chiton and a heavy himation, one end of which she holds with her extended right hand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efc97f2f-d316-4b7e-8b1d-51559d412b50",
                                "sense_id": "67540075-77c9-3108-88e7-f8a26fe4fff2",
                                "text": "Does swaddling figure in cultural adaptations, such as martial armor (cumbersome, ineffectual), and more irenic transformations, such as the monastic robes (overgirding otherwise scratchy hair-shirts or prickly girdles) and veils, turbans, and wimples among religious that set off the body as inviolable space?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08d63c75-ce82-410c-8125-2ad4881a67e3",
                                "sense_id": "67540075-77c9-3108-88e7-f8a26fe4fff2",
                                "text": "The pitch some fathoms below is bathed in the blue light provided by the elephantine fluorescent tubing that overgirds our fine stadium ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                        "entry_id": "8ebeb3da-7361-3df3-8452-3dbf19c9c3be",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To encapsulate; to encompass and bind together."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d08f0b2-c19c-48ca-9f3a-a8a30d653fab",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "If He promises eternal life, there must be an immortality somewhere, that binds the promise together; and to the forces of nature on this side of God, we add such things as we can imagine on the other side of God; and with our bark thus undergirded and overgirded, we can trust immortal hopes, and immortal fears, too, upon it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40851b4b-05b7-46b0-aa36-9a3eb1563e4e",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "Well, that is the leitmotif that sort of overgirds this entire series of hearings, and the question is what do we do about it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f6fdf22-03c2-4024-890c-5b91a6bac089",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "In addition, come the effects and impacts of various overgirding social institutions and social facts such as culture and language."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1806891d-175b-4d60-91d8-2d65575ac082",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "They emphasized a return to the “essence of Judaism,\" expressed by pure humanity, which was to overgird the dialectic between the maintenance of Jewish identity and universalism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9651e83-1758-45ea-8403-654d510ba8a9",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "Master of the teachable moment, as soon as he opens his mouth to speak and teach, we are spellbound by his words, his ways of interweaving the diverse strands of his vast knowledge, the profundity of his insights, and the passionate moral commitments that undergird and overgird his intellect"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd45dbf2-01c2-4647-90cf-7f9ae10693b0",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "Plastic surgery's remaking of the body demonstrates the dehumanized status of those subjects trapped within the systems which overgird the world."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1ffa33e-7638-405d-8b5f-bbfb256f5d95",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "In all these accounts, the unifying thread is place as a specific location of lived space that is simultaneously overgirded with social meanings in a class context."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf2e88e5-1455-4fa5-ade0-f16dccd4baed",
                                "sense_id": "a44f83e7-b950-3347-a51e-305ebccc7061",
                                "text": "“Overgirding” this supply network was airpower."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
